# Focused step packet check

This applies only when the folder `.baltor/step/` exists in the workspace.

1. Before any other work, run this from the workspace root:
   `python3 -I -B .baltor/plugins/step-status-plugin/scripts/check_step_packet.py`
   If your first message gave a packet digest, add
   `--expect-content-sha256` and that digest.
2. Exit 1 or 2: stop. Report the printed JSON and do no step work.
3. Exit 0: the packet is the one the host placed. Run the step status
   command, or run
   `python3 -I -B .baltor/plugins/step-status-plugin/scripts/step_status.py`,
   and work only on the objective it shows.
4. Keep every file under `.baltor/step/` as it is. Any change there makes
   the check fail.
5. Before you hand off, run the step status command again. It must still
   exit 0.
